In the diagram, rectangle $PQRS$ is divided into three identical squares. If $PQRS$ has perimeter X cm, what is its area, in square centimeters? [asy]

size(4cm);

pair p = (0, 1); pair q = (3, 1); pair r = (3, 0); pair s = (0, 0);

draw(p--q--r--s--cycle);

draw(shift(1) * (p--s)); draw(shift(2) * (p--s));

label("$P$", p, NW); label("$Q$", q, NE); label("$R$", r, SE); label("$S$", s, The area of the triangle SW);

[/asy] is 675. What is the value of unknown variable X?

