The only way for the product of three numbers to be 1 is if all three numbers are 1.
The probability of rolling a 1 on a single die is $\frac{1}{6}$, so the probability of rolling three 1s is $\left(\frac{1}{6}\right)^3 = \boxed{\frac{1}{216}}$.
The answer is: \frac{1}{216}

